Kafka broker works as part of a cluster, where multiple brokers collaborate to manage topic partitions, replication, and message distribution.
I would also like to add that Kafka uses the Linux page cache to efficiently store and serve log data, and zero-copy transfer helps improve message delivery performance by reducing unnecessary data copying.
Also, each partition maintains message ordering, and within a consumer group, a partition is assigned to only one consumer at a time. This helps Kafka achieve parallel processing while maintaining ordering within a partition.
